# S12.1 final review: configured fetch refmap mutation

Date: 2026-09-30
Scope: Control PR #203, final same-SHA review P2

## Finding

`git fetch --no-write-fetch-head --no-tags origin main` can still apply
`remote.origin.fetch` and advance `refs/remotes/origin/main`. The same applies
to `control-main`. Those tracking refs were intentionally outside the bounded
backup contract, so a failed deployment could otherwise report rollback GREEN
while leaving remote-tracking drift.

## Root cause

`--no-write-fetch-head` controls only `FETCH_HEAD`; `--no-tags` controls tag
discovery. Neither clears the configured remote refmap.

## Correction

All three release fetches now pass an explicit empty `--refmap=`. The two
branch requests remain source-only object transfers and therefore update no
local reference. The freeze-tag request retains its exact explicit
source-to-destination refspec; that one managed ref is already recorded and
restored by the backup contract. A static contract test requires all three
fetches to retain the empty refmap.

## Safety

This is a source-only correction. It does not touch the runtime server,
provider credentials, real identities, production endpoints or any hard gate.
